# Subsystem ownership.
#
# The target is TWO owners on every path, so that no subsystem is one person's
# absence away from being unmaintained. That is not the current state: this
# project has one maintainer, and every line below says so honestly rather than
# listing a second name that does not exist.
#
# GRVX-1210 §6 step 1 is explicit that granting rights to somebody who has not
# met the ladder criteria, in order to improve this file, is the wrong move.
# MAINTAINERS.md records the real bus factor, and scripts/audit_access.sh
# reports `bus factor 1 remains on <path>` for every line here with one owner.
#
# When a second maintainer is granted rights, their subsystems are added here as
# part of the onboarding checklist — see docs/oss/maintainer-onboarding.md.

# Everything, unless a more specific rule below matches.
*                        @lgreene03

# --- Correctness. The numbers Gravix's claims rest on. --------------------
/schemas/                @lgreene03
/pkg/recompute/          @lgreene03
/pkg/sketch/             @lgreene03
/pkg/lineage/            @lgreene03
/contracts/              @lgreene03
/tests/correctness/      @lgreene03

# --- Ingest and transform -------------------------------------------------
/services/ingestion/     @lgreene03
/transforms/             @lgreene03
/proto/                  @lgreene03

# --- Query and presentation ----------------------------------------------
/cube/                   @lgreene03
/dashboards/             @lgreene03
/services/gateway/       @lgreene03
# The gateway's implementation, moved out of services/gateway/ by GRVX-1302 so a
# second entrypoint can compose with it. services/gateway/ is now five lines.
/pkg/gatewaycore/        @lgreene03

# --- Operations -----------------------------------------------------------
/deploy/                 @lgreene03
/scripts/                @lgreene03
/.github/                @lgreene03

# --- Governance and planning ---------------------------------------------
/docs/oss/               @lgreene03
/docs/04-non-goals.md    @lgreene03
/GOVERNANCE.md           @lgreene03
/MAINTAINERS.md          @lgreene03

# --- The commercial tier --------------------------------------------------
#
# /ee/ deliberately keeps a single owner while the paid tier is small. That is a
# known bus-factor gap, recorded in MAINTAINERS.md rather than papered over: a
# second owner here is a licence and revenue question as much as a code one.
/ee/                     @lgreene03

# --- Custody, which is NOT granted with merge access ----------------------
#
# Organisation ownership, billing, DNS, publishing credentials and ee/ signing
# keys are held separately on purpose, so that a compromised maintainer account
# cannot take the project's identity. They appear in no CODEOWNERS line because
# they are not paths in this repository. See GRVX-1503.
